Subject: src/vmsjobs.c: pass the pid of the struct child to LIB$SPAWN

Since 4.4 child_execute_job() takes a struct childbase, which has no pid
member (only struct child has), so the LIB$SPAWN calls that store the
subprocess's pid in child->pid no longer compile (%CC-E-NEEDMEMBER).  On
VMS it is only called from start_job_command() with a struct child (the
callers in main.c and function.c are for other systems), and
vmsHandleChildTerm() already casts it back; do the same here.

--- a/src/vmsjobs.c	2026-10-05 00:08:18.059026213 +0100
+++ b/src/vmsjobs.c	2026-10-05 00:08:18.075557114 +0100
@@ -1407,7 +1407,7 @@
                      NULL, /* output-file */
                      &spflags,                                 /* flags */
                      &pnamedsc,                                /* proc name */
-                     &child->pid, &child->cstatus, &child->efn,
+                     &((struct child *)child)->pid, &child->cstatus, &child->efn,
                      0, 0,
                      0, 0, 0);
 
@@ -1423,7 +1423,7 @@
                       NULL,
                       &spflags,
                       &pnamedsc,
-                      &child->pid, &child->cstatus, &child->efn,
+                      &((struct child *)child)->pid, &child->cstatus, &child->efn,
                       vmsHandleChildTerm, child,
                       0, 0, 0);
    status = child->vms_launch_status;
